      "problem": "If ${6}^{t}=\\frac{1}{36},$ then $t=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite $36$ as ${6}^{2}$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ {6}^{t} & =\\frac{1}{{6}^{2}} \\\\ {6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(6)$, we equate the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{t} & ={6}^{-2} \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=-2.$",
